Spec: Authenticated backend transport authority

Purpose:
  Carry actual device and Agent application identity through backend control, publication and visitor admission.

Owns:
  ./transport_gate.go
  ./transport_gate_test.go

References:
  ./identity.sdd
  ./store.sdd

Must:
  Obtain identity only from actual standard server-side device mTLS under the configured owner root and fixed ALPN, followed by an exact bounded Agent scope preface.
  Keep peer, control and service authorization objects privately bound to one gate; request fields cannot construct proof.
  Bind every control RunID to device revision, application and publish/access role; reject empty or borrowed RunIDs.
  Publish only owner-approved fixed service scopes with deterministic opaque proxy names and current device/service generations.
  Admit visitors only with a fresh exact-scope grant and retain an active authorization cancellation handle for both relay and actual hole-punching.
  Reserve separate bounded query lanes for waiting hole-punch visitors and their control/publisher replies, with at most eight calls per control per lane.
  Bound peers, controls, publications and active authorizations; expire pending peers and stopped or stale controls without blocking on storage.
  Recheck current authority every five hundred milliseconds and cancel affected operations on revocation or storage failure; keep a separate monotonic expiry path while storage is blocked.
  Use fixed errors without logging inputs, scopes, certificates or addresses; close owned sockets on failure and stop.
  Stop owned network resources immediately and expose a separate context-bounded worker-drain wait so blocked storage cannot hang socket shutdown.
  Expose only aggregate in-process counts for owned runtime readiness checks, without a new unauthenticated metrics listener.
  Bind each active authorization handle to its exact publication name and transport kind.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Verify actual device-authenticated backend authority and current scoped cancellation.
